  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Peraton Enterprise Solutions obligated $635M in FY2026 to date. Peraton Enterprise Solutions won 111 federal awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $5.7M and obligations down 35.2% year over year. Peraton Enterprise Solutions obligations by fiscal year were $1.4B in FY21, $967M in FY22, $1.1B in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, and $980M in FY25, showing a higher run rate in prior years compared with the current fiscal year. Peraton Enterprise Solutions concentration is evident across a few agencies and markets: the General Services Administration obligated $209M, the Department of Defense obligated $127M, and Computer Systems Design Services accounted for $492M of obligations. Peraton Enterprise Solutions also recorded activity with the Department of the Treasury, Department of Homeland Security, and Department of Health and Human Services. Peraton Enterprise Solutions includes some corrective or negative obligation entries in the current fiscal year totals, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is ongoing.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies are the largest buyers of Peraton Enterprise Solutions?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, obligating $209M. The Department of Defense follows with $127M. The Department of the Treasury obligated $75.9M, the Department of Homeland Security obligated $68.1M, and the Department of Health and Human Services obligated $65.1M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which markets account for most of Peraton Enterprise Solutions' obligations?",
        "body": "Computer Systems Design Services is the largest market, with $492M in obligations. Electronic Computer Manufacturing represents $75.9M and Other Computer Related Services represents $43.4M. Peraton Enterprise Solutions also has obligations in Computing Infrastructure Providers, Data Processing, Web Hosting, and Related Services at $24.3M."
      }
    ]
  },
